{"id": "EUVD-2025-208840", "enisaUuid": "0dfe2b91-9914-39ae-951a-64073e6ce2e4", "description": "In the Linux kernel, the following vulnerability has been resolved:\n\nbtrfs: fix reservation leak in some error paths when inserting inline extent\n\nIf we fail to allocate a path or join a transaction, we return from\n__cow_file_range_inline() without freeing the reserved qgroup data,\nresulting in a leak. Fix this by ensuring we call btrfs_qgroup_free_data()\nin such cases.", "datePublished": "2026-03-18T17:40:58", "dateUpdated": "2026-10-19T18:25:25", "baseScore": 7.5, "baseScoreVersion": "3.1", "baseScoreVector": "CVSS:3.1/AV:N/AC:L/PR:N/UI:N/S:U/C:N/I:N/A:H", "references": ["https://git.kernel.org/stable/c/f7156512c8166d385f574b9ec030479aa7b1e8c9", "https://git.kernel.org/stable/c/28b97fcbbf523779688e8de5fe55bf2dae3859f6", "https://git.kernel.org/stable/c/f3ee1732851aec6fe6b2cec2ef1b32d4e71d9913", "https://git.kernel.org/stable/c/28768bd3abf9995a93f6e01bfce01c60622964dd", "https://git.kernel.org/stable/c/c1c050f92d8f6aac4e17f7f2230160794fceef0c"], "aliases": ["CVE-2025-71268", "GHSA-62m8-jj4j-qm8p"], "assigner": "Linux", "epss": 0.23, "enisaIdProduct": [{"id": "1dca96ab-ffe1-347c-b482-85dba86f1398", "product": {"name": "Linux", "vendor": {"name": "Linux"}}, "product_version": "94ed938aba557aa798acf496f09afb289b619fcd <f3ee1732851aec6fe6b2cec2ef1b32d4e71d9913"}, {"id": "2509fcd0-9409-3d80-b141-327c27f1ff94", "product": {"name": "Linux", "vendor": {"name": "Linux"}}, "product_version": "94ed938aba557aa798acf496f09afb289b619fcd <f7156512c8166d385f574b9ec030479aa7b1e8c9"}, {"id": "4ec11734-59bd-38c6-9698-530c2d3053da", "product": {"name": "Linux", "vendor": {"name": "Linux"}}, "product_version": "patch: 6.18.10"}, {"id": "538adec6-d3b8-3e7e-a173-bba0e9850d9d", "product": {"name": "Linux", "vendor": {"name": "Linux"}}, "product_version": "94ed938aba557aa798acf496f09afb289b619fcd <28b97fcbbf523779688e8de5fe55bf2dae3859f6"}, {"id": "8a35fc6a-45c5-3d0d-9361-a712331a31e4", "